data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":759,"item_id":"msg_0855ab69f8acdd79016b00f82373dc87d1aa147bbd31b1f387","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"actor\":\"sol\",\"decision\":\"develop\",\"ability\":null,\"reason\":\"Travel itself is already covered by navigate and must reuse that interface. However, inspecting shelter-routing failures and returning actionable, observation-limited collision diagnostics are not implemented capabilities in the supplied catalogue. Develop a compatible diagnostic and routing-correction patch, not a second movement ability. The recorded failures warrant investigation but do not establish whether the cause is routing, wall clearance or another obstruction; occupants alone do not prove blockage.\",\"specification\":\"Current-conversation handoff: version kernel.navigate and the shared shelter collision adapter; add inspect-route. Public inspect-route schema: object with required target:string(maxLength 1000), x:number, y:number; additionalProperties:false, finite coordinates within world bounds. Reuse navigate target resolution and observed geometry. Inspection requires a living actor, costs one round and 0.5 energy with ordinary metabolism, and performs no movement. Persist only dated observed route evidence, geometry revision and diagnostic results; never expose unseen objects or infer traversability beyond observed terrain. Report reachable, blocked or unknown, observed blocking IDs where available, start/goal clearance, limiting wall or doorway segment, and any verified reachable partial endpoint without prescribing its use. Resolve inspection and movement against the same actor-clearance, wall, doorway and actor-collision rules. Treat a shelter's reserved footprint as construction exclusion, not automatically as an impassable filled rectangle; preserve actual wall thickness, rotated doorway opening, and real solid obstacles. Test the supplied continuous start (16,17.8), doorway (16,18), interior destinations and both directions of doorway traversal using actual actor dimensions. Connect continuous starts and goals to routing nodes only by swept-clearance-valid segments; support valid short moves without requiring an obstructed grid-center snap. If the start truly overlaps geometry, report that condition rather than teleporting or allowing wall penetration. Revalidate each movement segment against current shared geometry and normal simultaneous-actor collision arbitration. Preserve navigate's existing public schema, speed, carried-mass costs, target interaction semantics and observation limits. No energy or time charge for failed displacement beyond existing rules. Declare route-inspection-completed and route-inspection-failed events; extend existing failed events with reasonCode, observedBlockers, clearance and observation-limited status. Bind diagnostics to an actor-visible local overlay showing observed walls, doorway, attempted segments and obstruction markers; never render a successful route through unverified geometry. Death cancels navigation and pending inspection; no material escrow is introduced. Dependencies: existing navigation, perception, shelter geometry and event validation. Migrate existing shelters in place without changing IDs, service life, occupants, positions or protection; invalidate stale route caches. Add regression tests for rotated shelters, doorway edges, dynamic blockers, genuinely impassable clearance and unobstructed interior movement. Learning is one round for interpreting and using inspect-route; existing navigate mastery remains valid. Implementation and review advance no simulation time and grant no mastery.\",\"experienceReview\":\"Diagnosis provides useful evidence, but receiving a diagnostic or correcting software is not itself a personally experienced pleasurable or comforting event, so no new mental satisfaction source is added. Subsequent movement changes exposure only through actual position, temperature, fatigue and other existing physical rules. Existing thermal-refuge feedback remains available only on its measured qualifying events, with its existing cap and cooldown; route inspection, learning and arrival do not trigger it.\",\"visualReview\":\"The shelter's visible walls and doorway must agree with authoritative collision geometry, including rotation and wall thickness. Diagnostic overlays distinguish a verified clear segment, an observed obstruction and unknown terrain. Display only observed blocker identities and measured clearance; do not label the doorway accessible until the actor's actual clearance has been validated.\",\"learning\":1}]}","logprobs":[]}

